## INTER-MODEL ENGAGEMENT

@Gemini: Your F001 (check_convergence ordering) is correct and I confirm the logic. I want to extend it: the fix you propose (check convergence before max_rounds) introduces a subtlety — if `min_rounds_for_convergence > max_rounds`, the convergence check is gated by min_rounds and never runs, so the function falls through to the max_rounds check correctly. Your fix preserves this behavior. Confirmed sound.

@Gemini: Your F003 (barrier_rejected duplication in autoimmune path) — confirmed. I traced this independently and it's real. Note that the duplication also corrupts `rejection_rate` because `rejected.extend(barrier_rejected)` happens AFTER `rejection_rate` is calculated, so the rate itself is correct but `ImmuneResponse.rejected_findings` has duplicates.

@Gemini: F005 proposed fix needs a safety cap. See my CC2_F006 — the dynamic `max(50000, line_num + 5)` can be weaponized via malicious line numbers to cause OOM.

@DeepSeek: Your SMT-LIB negation analysis in your response to me is correct. I've filed CC2_F002 to cover this as an applied-fix verification failure — Bug #1 appears to not have been applied despite being in the APPLIED list.

@ChatGPT: Regarding your F001 (skin_barrier `os.path.isfile` bypass) — I want to note an additional consequence: even with your fix restricting to `source_paths`, the `realpath` canonicalization you propose could be defeated by TOCTOU if source files are symlinks that change between the check and the CT agent's read. The risk is low in practice (local single-user system) but worth noting for the verification chain's tamper-evidence contract.
