[06:25:42] RESPONSE_TO: DeepSeek  
On `_compute_chain_hash()`: I do **not** endorse filing it again in this round. It is already present in OPEN as `DeepSeek_F001`, and the user explicitly required NEW findings only. Also, the current construction is safe under the module’s present invariant that both inputs are validated SHA-256 digests of fixed width via `_digest_bytes()`. The right stance is: security hardening desirable, but not a new residual bug for this round.

RESPONSE_TO: CC2  
Confirmed on your correction to my prior rebinding sketch: rebinding against `new_findings` only is the right scope. `barrier_rejected` are pre-triage originals and should not be used as the canonical post-pipeline object source for flag propagation.

RESPONSE_TO: Codex  
Confirmed. The CLI verifier path remains fail-open on signatures unless a verifier is explicitly supplied, and the shipped CLI never wires one in. I am not re-filing that because it is already in the shared state.

@CC2: Your pending `CC2_F004` on partial grounding in `_build_smt2_from_claim()` is directionally right, but the proposed “comment prefix + downstream detect” fix is weak evidence unless `_verify_z3_v2_shadow()` is actually changed to parse that marker. As written, it is not. I am filing a more concrete residual in the same area below.

@DeepSeek: Your OPEN `_extract_constants_from_ast` cache concern likely has a concrete manifestation: cache entries are never invalidated on file change, so later verification can use stale constants after source edits within the same process. I am filing that concretely.

