    "DESCRIPTION": "FIND: `bench/immune_agents.py`, `_build_smt2_from_claim()`. Conjunction-of-negations produces false confirmations for grounded multi-condition claims. When a claim contains multiple comparisons on the same grounded variable (e.g., 'x > 0 AND x < 10' with x grounded to 15), each condition is negated independently as separate `(assert (not ...))` statements. SMT-LIB treats multiple asserts as conjunction. The resulting formula is `x=15 AND NOT(x>0) AND NOT(x<10)` = `x=15 AND x<=0 AND x>=10`, which is trivially UNSAT (can't simultaneously be <=0 and >=10 and =15). The solver returns UNSAT_GROUNDED → CONFIRMED with 0.85 confidence. But the original claim '15 > 0 AND 15 < 10' is FALSE (15 < 10 fails). The correct negation is `NOT(x>0 AND x<10)` = `x<=0 OR x>=10`, encoded as a single `(assert (or (not (> x 0)) (not (< x 10))))`. With x=15: `15<=0 OR 15>=10` = TRUE → SAT → REJECTED. This is a concrete false confirmation path. Bug #1 (applied fix) was about this class of issue; the fix appears incomplete for the grounded-variable case.",
