**Definitive stance:** Five findings filed. CC2_F001 is the highest-impact: false confirmations from conjunction-of-negations in grounded SMT-LIB proofs — a concrete, exploitable correctness flaw with an exact counterexample. CC2_F002 fixes a semantic error in the reconciliation gate where UNCERTAIN is treated as counter-evidence. CC2_F003 and CC2_F005 harden the SymPy/SMT-LIB translation pipeline against edge-case inputs. CC2_F004 corrects a reporting contract violation. All findings are complementary to the round 9 consensus; none conflict with existing CLOSED or PENDING work.
