@ChatGPT: Your F001 (Stage 4/5 ordering — duplicates can never contribute verified fixes) is architecturally sound. One question: does your proposed fix interact with CC2_R14_F002 (reconciliation gate lock enforcement)? If a duplicate finding's fix is verified and propagated to the canonical finding, and that canonical finding was previously REJECTED by both pipelines (locked), should the verified fix unlock it?

